{"step_index":155,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T17:38:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-07T23:08:45+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-07T23:08:45+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 69\n1: # JanaSeva - Public Grievance and Civic Issue Reporting System\n2: ### VTU Community Project (1BCP308)\n3: \n4: ---\n5: \n6: ## 📌 Project Overview\n7: **JanaSeva** is a responsive web application designed to empower citizens and college students to report local civic issues (potholes, dark streetlights, garbage overflow, water leaks, and clogged drainage) and track real-time resolution with local municipal authorities.\n8: \n9: Developed as part of the **VTU 3rd Semester Community Project (1BCP308)** curriculum.\n10: \n11: ---\n12: \n13: ## 🚀 Two Ways to Run the Project\n14: \n15: ### Option 1: Instant 1-Click Browser Demo (Zero Setup Required)\n16: If you have a project presentation today and don't want to install tools:\n17: 1. Locate the file `civic_portal.html` in this folder.\n18: 2. Double-click it to open it in **Google Chrome** or **Microsoft Edge**.\n19: 3. The entire website is 100% interactive! You can:\n20:    - File grievances with photo previews.\n21:    - Track tickets (`TKT-8941`, `TKT-8938`, etc.).\n22:    - Filter issues by category and status.\n23:    - Print the project report card.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ### Option 2: Running with React + Vite (Professional Setup)\n28: When you want to demonstrate the React + Vite code to your professors:\n29: 1. **Install Node.js** (LTS version) from [nodejs.org](https://nodejs.org).\n30: 2. Open terminal inside the project folder:\n31:    ```bash\n32:    npm install\n33:    npm run dev\n34:    ```\n35: 3. Open the link displayed (usually `http://localhost:5173`) in your browser.\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 🎯 Features Aligned with VTU 1BCP308 Requirements\n40: 1. **Public Grievance Lodging**:\n41:    - Supports 6 civic categories: Potholes, Garbage, Streetlights, Water Leaks, Drainage, Sanitation.\n42:    - General landmark / area localization (protects citizen safety).\n43:    - Real photo evidence upload with instant preview.\n44:    - Auto-generated tracking ticket code (e.g. `TKT-8942`).\n45: \n46: 2. **Public Status Tracking**:\n47:    - 3-stage visual progress stepper: **Submitted → In Progress → Resolved**.\n48:    - Inspection log and official ward officer notes.\n49: \n50: 3. **Public Transparency Feed**:"}
